Sending keys: ['cat > attack.py << \'PYEOF\'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport random\nimport feal\n\ndef attack(encrypt_fn):\n    """\n    Chosen plaintext differential attack to recover key[5].\n\n    Cipher structure (4-round FEAL-like):\n      - After whitening and pre-mixing, Feistel rounds use key[2..5].\n      - Ciphertext: C_left = R4, C_right = R3 ^ R4  =>  R3 = C_left ^ C_right.\n      - L3 = C_left ^ f(R3 ^ key[5]).\n\n    Differential:  DeltaP = 0x8080000080800000  =>  DeltaR2 = 0x02000000 (deterministic).\n    Since L3 = R2, we have DeltaL3 = 0x02000000.\n\n    For each pair (P, P^DeltaP) with ciphertexts (C, C*):\n      f(R3 ^ k5) ^ f(R3* ^ k5) = (C_left ^ C_left*) ^ 0x02000000\n\n    key[5] is derived from a 16-bit seed: key[5] = (seed * 1234567) & 0xFFFFFFFF.\n    We brute force all 65536 seeds and filter with a few pairs.\n    """\n    f = feal.f_function\n    delta_p = 0x8080000080800000\n    delta_l3 = 0x02000000\n\n    # Generate chosen plaintext pairs and precompute check values\n    pairs = []\n    for _ in range(8):\n        pl = random.randint(0, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n        pr = random.randint(0, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n        p = (pl << 32) | pr\n        c = encrypt_fn(p)\n        cs = encrypt_fn(p ^ delta_p)\n\n        cl = (c >> 32) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        cr = c & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        cls = (cs >> 32) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        crs = cs & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n        r3 = cl ^ cr\n        r3s = cls ^ crs\n        target = (cl ^ cls) ^ delta_l3\n        pairs.append((r3, r3s, target))\n\n    # Brute force over all 16-bit seeds\n    for seed in range(65536):\n        k5 = (seed * 1234567) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        ok = True\n        for r3, r3s, target in pairs:\n            if (f(r3 ^ k5) ^ f(r3s ^ k5)) != target:\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if ok:\n            return k5\n\n    raise RuntimeError("key[5] not found")\nPYEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.1 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
